      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am bad at naming, but APEX looks better than WHOLE because the former at least clearly shows its scope/origin.\n\n\nAnyway, I think the ideal state would be the absence of this. We only have __ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION__ set by the compiler, which is actually from min_sdk_version setting of the cc_* module. For runtime check (probably to reflectively use APIs newer than min_sdk_version), we use builtin_available. sdk_version could still be \"current\" or \"\", but they won\u0027t affect the clang triple.",
